# TypeScript Advanced Patterns

## Utility Types

### Built-in TypeScript Utility Types

```typescript
// Partial - make all properties optional
type PartialEvent = Partial<Event>;

// Required - make all properties required
type RequiredEvent = Required<PartialEvent>;

// Pick - select specific properties
type EventPreview = Pick<Event, 'id' | 'title' | 'date'>;

// Omit - exclude specific properties
// Prefer Except from type-fest for stricter type safety
type EventWithoutDates = Omit<Event, 'createdAt' | 'updatedAt'>;
// Better: import { Except } from 'type-fest';
// type EventWithoutDates = Except<Event, 'createdAt' | 'updatedAt'>;

// Extract - extract union members
type StringKeys = Extract<keyof Event, string>;

// Exclude - exclude union members
type NonStringKeys = Exclude<keyof Event, string>;
```

## Type-Fest Utility Types

**Type-fest is the primary source for advanced utility types. Always prefer type-fest utilities over custom implementations.**

### Core Type-Fest Utilities

```typescript
import {
  PartialDeep,
  RequiredDeep,
  ReadonlyDeep,
  Writable,
  WritableDeep,
  SetRequired,
  SetOptional,
  SetNonNullable,
  RequireAtLeastOne,
  RequireExactlyOne,
  RequireAllOrNone,
  Except,
} from 'type-fest';

// Deep partial - make all nested properties optional
type PartialEventConfig = PartialDeep<EventConfig>;

// Deep required - make all nested properties required
type RequiredEventConfig = RequiredDeep<EventConfig>;

// Deep readonly - make all nested properties readonly
type ImmutableEvent = ReadonlyDeep<Event>;

// Remove readonly modifiers (shallow)
type MutableEvent = Writable<Readonly<Event>>;

// Remove readonly modifiers (deep)
type MutableEventDeep = WritableDeep<ReadonlyDeep<Event>>;

// Make specific keys required
type EventWithRequiredId = SetRequired<Partial<Event>, 'id'>;
type UpdateEventData = SetRequired<Partial<Event>, 'id'>;

// Make specific keys optional
type EventWithOptionalDates = SetOptional<Event, 'createdAt' | 'updatedAt'>;

// Make specific keys non-nullable
type EventWithNonNullTitle = SetNonNullable<Event, 'title'>;

// Stricter Omit alternative - prevents accidental extra properties
type EventWithoutDates = Except<Event, 'createdAt' | 'updatedAt'>;
```

### Advanced Type-Fest Utilities

```typescript
import {
  RequireAtLeastOne,
  RequireExactlyOne,
  RequireAllOrNone,
} from 'type-fest';

// Require at least one property (useful for search forms)
interface SearchOptions {
  query?: string;
  tags?: string[];
  category?: string;
}
type ValidSearch = RequireAtLeastOne<SearchOptions>;

// Valid: at least one property present
const search1: ValidSearch = { query: 'typescript' };
const search2: ValidSearch = { tags: ['a', 'b'] };
const search3: ValidSearch = { query: 'ts', tags: ['a'] };

// Invalid: no properties
// const invalidSearch: ValidSearch = {}; // Error

// Require exactly one property (mutually exclusive)
interface PaymentMethod {
  creditCard?: string;
  paypal?: string;
  bitcoin?: string;
}
type SinglePayment = RequireExactlyOne<PaymentMethod>;

// Valid: exactly one property
const pay1: SinglePayment = { creditCard: '1234' };
const pay2: SinglePayment = { paypal: 'user@example.com' };

// Invalid: multiple or none
// const invalidPay1: SinglePayment = {}; // Error
// const invalidPay2: SinglePayment = { creditCard: '1234', paypal: 'user@example.com' }; // Error

// Require all or none (grouped properties)
interface UserProfile {
  username?: string;
  firstName?: string;
  lastName?: string;
}
type ProfileInfo = RequireAllOrNone<UserProfile, 'firstName' | 'lastName'>;

// Valid: all or none of the specified keys
const profile1: ProfileInfo = { username: 'testuser' };
const profile2: ProfileInfo = { username: 'testuser', firstName: 'John', lastName: 'Doe' };

// Invalid: only one of the group
// const invalidProfile: ProfileInfo = { username: 'testuser', firstName: 'John' }; // Error
```

### Custom Utility Types (Reference Only)

These are shown for educational purposes. In production, always use type-fest equivalents.

```typescript
// ❌ Custom implementation - use SetRequired from type-fest instead
type PartialExcept<T, K extends keyof T> = Partial<T> & Pick<T, K>;
// ✅ Use: SetRequired<Partial<T>, K>

// ❌ Custom implementation - use SetRequired from type-fest instead
type RequiredKeys<T, K extends keyof T> = T & Required<Pick<T, K>>;
// ✅ Use: SetRequired<T, K>

// ❌ Custom implementation - use PartialDeep from type-fest instead
type DeepPartial<T> = {
  [P in keyof T]?: T[P] extends object ? DeepPartial<T[P]> : T[P];
};
// ✅ Use: PartialDeep<T>
```

## Type Guards

### Type Predicates

```typescript
export function isEvent(value: unknown): value is Event {
  return (
    typeof value === 'object' &&
    value !== null &&
    'id' in value &&
    'title' in value &&
    'content' in value
  );
}

export function isEventArray(value: unknown): value is Event[] {
  return Array.isArray(value) && value.every(isEvent);
}

// Usage
function processEvent(data: unknown) {
  if (isEvent(data)) {
    // TypeScript knows data is Event here
    console.log(data.title);
  }
}
```

### Discriminated Unions

```typescript
type LoadingState = {
  status: 'loading';
};

type SuccessState<T> = {
  status: 'success';
  data: T;
};

type ErrorState = {
  status: 'error';
  error: Error;
};

type AsyncState<T> = LoadingState | SuccessState<T> | ErrorState;

function handleState<T>(state: AsyncState<T>) {
  switch (state.status) {
    case 'loading':
      return 'Loading...';
    case 'success':
      return `Data: ${state.data}`; // TypeScript knows data exists
    case 'error':
      return `Error: ${state.error.message}`; // TypeScript knows error exists
  }
}
```

## Generic Types

### Generic Functions

```typescript
// Generic function
export function identity<T>(value: T): T {
  return value;
}

// Generic with constraints
export function getProperty<T, K extends keyof T>(obj: T, key: K): T[K] {
  return obj[key];
}

// Generic with multiple constraints
export function merge<T extends object, U extends object>(a: T, b: U): T & U {
  return { ...a, ...b };
}
```

### Generic Components

```typescript
interface ListProps<T> {
  items: T[];
  renderItem: (item: T) => React.ReactNode;
  keyExtractor: (item: T) => string;
}

export function List<T>({ items, renderItem, keyExtractor }: ListProps<T>) {
  return (
    <ul>
      {items.map((item) => (
        <li key={keyExtractor(item)}>{renderItem(item)}</li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  );
}

// Usage
<List<Event>
  items={events}
  renderItem={(event) => <EventCard event={event} />}
  keyExtractor={(event) => event.id}
/>
```

### Generic Hooks

```typescript
export function useAsync<T>(
  asyncFunction: () => Promise<T>
): {
  data: T | null;
  isLoading: boolean;
  error: Error | null;
  execute: () => Promise<void>;
} {
  const [data, setData] = useState<T | null>(null);
  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(false);
  const [error, setError] = useState<Error | null>(null);

  const execute = useCallback(async () => {
    setIsLoading(true);
    setError(null);
    try {
      const result = await asyncFunction();
      setData(result);
    } catch (err) {
      setError(err instanceof Error ? err : new Error('Unknown error'));
    } finally {
      setIsLoading(false);
    }
  }, [asyncFunction]);

  return { data, isLoading, error, execute };
}
```

## Branded Types

```typescript
// Branded type for type safety
type UserId = string & { readonly __brand: unique symbol };
type EventId = string & { readonly __brand: unique symbol };

function createUserId(id: string): UserId {
  return id as UserId;
}

function createEventId(id: string): EventId {
  return id as EventId;
}

// Prevents mixing up IDs
function getUserById(id: UserId) {
  // ...
}

// Compile error - EventId cannot be assigned to UserId
getUserById(createEventId('123'));
```

## Template Literal Types

```typescript
// Template literal types
type EventStatus = 'draft' | 'published' | 'archived';
type EventAction = `event-${EventStatus}`;

// Result: 'event-draft' | 'event-published' | 'event-archived'

// Advanced template literals
type ApiRoute = `/api/${string}`;
type EventRoute = `/api/events/${string}`;
```

## Mapped Types

### Using Type-Fest for Mapped Types

```typescript
import { ReadonlyDeep, Writable, WritableDeep } from 'type-fest';

// Deep readonly - preferred over shallow Readonly<T>
type ImmutableEvent = ReadonlyDeep<Event>;

// Remove readonly modifiers (shallow)
type MutableEvent = Writable<Readonly<Event>>;

// Remove readonly modifiers (deep)
type MutableEventDeep = WritableDeep<ReadonlyDeep<Event>>;
```

### Basic Mapped Types (Built-in)

```typescript
// Make all properties readonly (shallow - prefer ReadonlyDeep for nested)
type ReadonlyEvent = {
  readonly [K in keyof Event]: Event[K];
};

// Make all properties optional and nullable
type NullableEvent = {
  [K in keyof Event]: Event[K] | null;
};

// Create type from union
type EventKeys = 'id' | 'title' | 'content';
type EventRecord = {
  [K in EventKeys]: string;
};
```

## Conditional Types

```typescript
// Conditional type
type NonNullable<T> = T extends null | undefined ? never : T;

// Extract return type
type ReturnType<T> = T extends (...args: any[]) => infer R ? R : never;

// Extract function parameters
type Parameters<T> = T extends (...args: infer P) => any ? P : never;

// Check if type is array
type IsArray<T> = T extends any[] ? true : false;
```

## Type Assertions

### Type Assertions (Use Sparingly)

```typescript
// Type assertion
const value = event as Event;

// Non-null assertion (avoid if possible)
const title = event!.title;

// Type guard is better
if (isEvent(event)) {
  const title = event.title; // Type-safe
}
```

## Interface vs Type

### When to Use Interface

```typescript
// Use interface for object shapes that might be extended
interface Event {
  id: string;
  title: string;
}

interface ExtendedEvent extends Event {
  category: string;
}

// Interface merging (useful for library types)
interface Window {
  customProperty: string;
}
```

### When to Use Type

```typescript
// Use type for unions, intersections, and complex types
type EventStatus = 'draft' | 'published' | 'archived';

type EventWithStatus = Event & { status: EventStatus };

type EventOrTask = Event | Task;

// Mapped types
type PartialEvent = Partial<Event>;
```

## Type Narrowing

```typescript
// typeof narrowing
function processValue(value: string | number) {
  if (typeof value === 'string') {
    // TypeScript knows value is string
    return value.toUpperCase();
  }
  // TypeScript knows value is number
  return value.toFixed(2);
}

// instanceof narrowing
function processError(error: Error | string) {
  if (error instanceof Error) {
    // TypeScript knows error is Error
    return error.message;
  }
  // TypeScript knows error is string
  return error;
}

// in operator narrowing
function processEvent(event: Event | Task) {
  if ('content' in event) {
    // TypeScript knows event is Event
    return event.content;
  }
  // TypeScript knows event is Task
  return event.description;
}
```

## Type-Safe Event Handlers

```typescript
// Generic event handler type
type EventHandler<T extends HTMLElement> = (event: React.SyntheticEvent<T>) => void;

export function Button({ onClick }: { onClick: EventHandler<HTMLButtonElement> }) {
  return <button onClick={onClick}>Click</button>;
}

// Form event handler
type FormSubmitHandler = (event: React.FormEvent<HTMLFormElement>) => void;

export function Form({ onSubmit }: { onSubmit: FormSubmitHandler }) {
  return <form onSubmit={onSubmit}>...</form>;
}
```

## Type-Safe API Responses

```typescript
// Generic API response type
interface ApiResponse<T> {
  data: T;
  status: number;
  message?: string;
}

// Generic API error
interface ApiError<T = unknown> {
  message: string;
  status: number;
  errors?: T;
}

// Type-safe API function
export function getEvent(id: string): Promise<ApiResponse<Event>> {
  return apiClient.get(`/api/events/${id}`);
}
```

### Type-Fest Best Practices

- **Always prefer type-fest utilities** over custom implementations
- Use `PartialDeep` instead of custom `DeepPartial`
- Use `RequiredDeep` for deeply required types
- Use `SetRequired` / `SetOptional` for precise control
- Use `RequireAtLeastOne` for form validation types
- Use `ReadonlyDeep` / `WritableDeep` for immutable types
- Prefer `Except` over `Omit` for stricter type safety
- Use `RequireExactlyOne` for mutually exclusive properties
- Use `RequireAllOrNone` for grouped optional properties

## TypeScript Checklist

- [ ] **Always prefer type-fest utilities** over custom implementations
- [ ] Use interfaces for object shapes that might be extended
- [ ] Use types for unions, intersections, and complex types
- [ ] Use built-in utility types (Partial, Pick) when appropriate
- [ ] Use `PartialDeep` / `RequiredDeep` for nested objects
- [ ] Use `SetRequired` / `SetOptional` for precise property control
- [ ] Use `Except` instead of `Omit` for stricter type safety
- [ ] Use `RequireAtLeastOne` for form validation types
- [ ] Use `ReadonlyDeep` / `WritableDeep` for immutable types
- [ ] Implement type guards for runtime type checking
- [ ] Use discriminated unions for state management
- [ ] Use generic types for reusable code
- [ ] Avoid type assertions when possible
- [ ] Use type narrowing instead of assertions
- [ ] Keep types close to their usage
- [ ] Export types from entities/types files
- [ ] Use branded types for type safety
- [ ] Leverage template literal types for string unions
